// {"files":[{"path":"\\\\?\\C:\\Users\\danie\\OneDrive\\github-repos\\drosemann\\README.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":31,"oldLines":7,"newStart":31,"newLines":7,"lines":[" After over 2,000 gaming videos I made 15 videos in the Theo Browne style, archived at https://github.com/drosemann/drosemann/tree/main/theo-browne-era-video-style"," All of my domains are with netcup: d5niel.de for my portfolio, which will run on ForgeCMS (https://github.com/drosemann/forgecms) in the future, shadowunity.de for my Minecraft server, and hosting-club.de, a former hosting forum."," For writing itself I use ed-docs, an offline-first Markdown workspace with ed/vi habits like i, a, Esc and :w: https://github.com/drosemann/ed-docs","-Over the years every hosting era also produced a forum or blog attempt, ten in total, and I finally merged all of them into one codebase: forum-for-nerds, a self-hosted Next.js forum plus blog running on pure Docker with SQLite for dev and MariaDB in prod. Ten dead forums walked in, one nerd forum walked out.","+Over the years every hosting era also produced a forum or blog attempt, ten in total, and I finally merged all of them into one codebase: forum-for-nerds (https://github.com/drosemann/forum-for-nerds), a self-hosted Next.js forum plus blog running on pure Docker with SQLite for dev and MariaDB in prod. Ten dead forums walked in, one nerd forum walked out."," For storage I ended up with OneDrive 365 Basic with 100 GB for 2 euros a month, after years of being convinced I'd never give Microsoft a cent, until the Windows and Samsung integration won me over."," Speed doesn't matter much to me, and if OneDrive ever offers a 500 GB cold archive tier on very slow old hard drives for one or two euros a month, I'd be the first customer, and I'd probably store all my photos there too since 100 GB is easily enough for me."," I never actually needed it, since I never used more than two or three GB, but now I just upload 30 GB so I can say I use it."]}]}]}
